      ],
      "source": "https://cityofredlicktx.com/about-us/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the late 1800s, the Red Lick Methodist Episcopal Church South, founded in 1885, became the town’s social hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofredlicktx.com/about-us/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1992, the town honored its heritage by placing a Texas Historical Commission marker at the Red Lick Methodist Church.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/red-lick-tx"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Red Lick sits just off Farm Road 2148 North, about seven miles west of Texarkana, with Interstate 30 brushing its southern edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
